Defects found:

- **Instrument reading a different copy**: line 25.  
  Exact input: run `C:\rapidmeta-ssot-shell\scripts\g1_runtime_census.py` after editing `C:\rapidmeta-ssot-shell\ABALOPARATIDE_OSTEO_AUTO_FULL_REVIEW.html`, with `F:\rapidmeta-ssot-shell\ABALOPARATIDE_OSTEO_AUTO_FULL_REVIEW.html` unchanged.  
  Consequence: the census reports the hardcoded `F:` copy, not the worktree being changed.

- **Check that cannot fail**: lines 86-92.  
  Exact input: filesystem state where none of the 12 `SAMPLE` files exists under `F:\rapidmeta-ssot-shell`.  
  Consequence: every page prints `FILE ABSENT`, no row is measured, and the script still exits zero.

- **Status code reporting the wrapper rather than the work**: line 73.  
  Exact input: a sampled HTML file containing `<script>throw new Error('boom')</script><div id="tab-protocol"></div>`.  
  Consequence: Chrome can exit zero while the page engine failed, so the script counts runtime failure as empty tab content.

- **Selector keyed too broadly**: line 100.  
  Exact input: `<div id="tab-protocol"><span id="tab-note"></span>` + `"x"` repeated 400 times + `<table></table></div><div id="tab-search"></div>`.  
  Consequence: `id="tab-note"` is treated as the next tab boundary, truncating real protocol content to a false `-`.

- **Instrument reads markup text as occupancy**: lines 99 and 103.  
  Exact input: `<div id="tab-protocol" data-x="` + `"x"` repeated 400 times + `"><table></table></div><div id="tab-search"></div>`.  
  Consequence: attribute text is counted as panel text because the slice starts at `id=`, so an empty tab can become `H`.

- **Zero conflated with absent / off-by-one**: line 117.  
  Exact input: `st == ['H','H','H','H','H','H',' ','-']`.  
  Consequence: a missing seventh tab counts as “all 7 present tabs held,” while the eighth configured tab is ignored.

Not found: string-fix probe, idempotency guard, CRLF/LF text comparison, negation-dropped sentence parser.  
